pan><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T15:31:29-07:00","id":1483406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1481679-belial-s-brood-2e-tweaks-and-houserules?p=1482053#post1482053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like this! Manifestations are a fun idea that really didn't need the whole Ritual Discipline treatment, and I think your version works much better for Storyteller characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I'm glad you like it!<br /> <br /> And I agree. I am not really sure why the Brood ended up so player facing in <b>Spilled Blood</b>. Maybe it was intended as a stealthy way to let players keep playing their characters when they hit Humanity 0?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T16:12:53-07:00","id":1483413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1481679-belial-s-brood-2e-tweaks-and-houserules?p=1483406#post1483406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, I'm glad you like it!<br /> <br /> And I agree. I am not really sure why the Brood ended up so player facing in <b>Spilled Blood</b>. Maybe it was intended as a stealthy way to let players keep playing their characters when they hit Humanity 0?</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to remember the directive being that they should be antagonist only (note how they don't have sample character concepts). I don't think there was anything wrong with doing their powers up as rituals, but in hindsight, the execution doesn't quite work, at least in the sense that they don't work if you assume the Storyteller is bothering to roll such things out, which depends on the ST (I definitely wouldn't bother if I were running them vanilla). That said, Triadic Evolution is a REALLY cool idea, but a more simple and brutal approach to its systems is definitely the way to go for its systems. Even so, I generally prefer this version of the Brood to the Gnostic Satanists of 1E. <b>Belial's Brood </b>is a <i>deeply </i>weird book, in both good and bad ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T16:50:53-07:00","id":1483420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1481679-belial-s-brood-2e-tweaks-and-houserules?p=1483413#post1483413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even so, I generally prefer this version of the Brood to the Gnostic Satanists of 1E. <b>Belial's Brood </b>is a <i>deeply </i>weird book, in both good and bad ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>What were the bad ways?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T18:21:36-07:00","id":1483430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1481679-belial-s-brood-2e-tweaks-and-houserules?p=1483420#post1483420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What were the bad ways?</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer not to harp on about older material, but if I had to nail down an issue, I'd say that the systems in <b>Belial's Brood </b>are baroquely complicated. Every system has a subsystem, and each subsystem has a subsubsystem, and all of them are hidden within reams and reams and reams and reams of really dense prose. Nothing is concise. I have other issues, but every time I tried to figure out how Brood characters were supposed to work, I gave up after hunting for one too many minor details hidden in blocky paragraphs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual 