-gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1481679-belial-s-brood-2e-tweaks-and-houserules?p=1483413#post1483413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even so, I generally prefer this version of the Brood to the Gnostic Satanists of 1E. <b>Belial's Brood </b>is a <i>deeply </i>weird book, in both good and bad ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that might explain why they ended up with a ritual Discipline. Even though the 2e Brood is completely different, if their cool powers in 1e involved any sort of ritual [I've never read <b>Belial's Brood</b>], then I'd guess that Triadic Evolution was meant to bring those blood rite vibes forward, even though the new Brood is something completely different.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}